			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				123,
				10
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Refactor file structure to enforce PascalCase directory hierarchy\n\nRename all flat-file modules under `Source/Function` and `Source/Workbench` to nested directories that strictly adhere to the PascalCase naming convention required by the CodeEditorLand architecture. This structural migration transforms flat files like `BuildVSCode.ts` into `Build/VS/Code.ts` and `SkyBridge.ts` into `Sky/Bridge.ts`, ensuring consistent directory organization that mirrors the semantic hierarchy of the component names.\n\nNo logic, behavior, or code content has been altered; this is a pure refactoring of the filesystem layout. The change aligns the `Sky` element's source tree with the project's strict naming standards for modules and file paths, improving navigability and consistency across the codebase.",
			"SHA": "1d053ed13259bce01d5f344f17064c0af2f95213"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:26:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				106,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Normalize spacing in conditional block for openView call\n\nReformat the multi-line condition check and function invocation for `Services.Views.openView` in SkyBridge. Align the closing brace of the `if` condition with the opening keyword and place the `catch` handler on a single line to match the project's consistent formatting style.\n\nThis change affects only whitespace and line breaks within the `Source/Function/SkyBridge.ts` file. It does not alter the logic, execution flow, or behavior of the view reopening mechanism, but ensures visual consistency with the surrounding codebase.",
			"SHA": "bf7d69c858bc72a49df69ed4317bb51de94b979c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T15:09:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				106,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Integrate real WebviewInput and implement pending HTML replay for race conditions\n\nReplace the static placeholder implementation in SkyBridge with a conditional path that attempts to instantiate a real workbench `WebviewInput` via `IWebviewWorkbenchService.openWebview`. This enables actual iframe rendering and message-port plumbing, falling back to the placeholder only if the service chain is unavailable.\n\nAddress race conditions where extension code sets `view.webview.html` synchronously during `resolveWebviewView` before the resolver is fully registered or the panel becomes visible. Implement a global pending HTML cache (`__CEL_WEBVIEW_PENDING_HTML__`) keyed by ViewId and Handle. Upon successful resolver registration, replay any cached HTML using the correct `setHtml` method signature preferred by the workbench, rather than relying on property assignment which previously no-opped on real workbench objects.\n\nAdd a defensive `openView` trigger to force re-evaluation of the WebviewViewPane's visibility state if a resolver registers after the pane has already activated, ensuring the `onDidChangeBodyVisibility` event fires and the new resolver is utilized. Update diagnostic logging to report whether HTML was applied via method, setter, or replayed from cache.",
			"SHA": "8f72913202b7d54bdffca1adaa514083dbd7c4bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T11:34:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				106,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add post-registration probe for WebviewView resolver map integrity\n\nInsert a diagnostic probe immediately after `register` call to verify the workbench's `_resolvers` map actually contains the new `ViewId`. This addresses a specific failure mode where registration completes silently but the `resolve` callback never fires, indicating the `WebviewViews` service instance used by SkyBridge is disjoint from the instance used by `WebviewViewPane` due to a dependency injection scope mismatch.\n\nThe probe checks both `_resolvers` and `_awaitingRevival` maps, emitting a structured diagnostic log to Mountain via the IPC channel. This confirms whether the bridge is talking to the correct service instance or if a DI scope issue is preventing view revival. Logs include map sizes and resolution status to differentiate between registration failure and resolver isolation.\n\nThis complements the existing entry-trace logging by validating the internal state of the workbench immediately after registration, providing a deterministic signal to triage 'register-success-but-no-resolve' bugs during extension host hot-reloads.",
			"SHA": "7fd7402cea849b697ef12e0ba0c6cedf8229a2d1"
		}
	],
